# --- Agent / local working files (never commit) ---
# Coding-agent config, instructions, and scratch notes are local-only. `git add -A`/
# `git add .` sweeps up anything not listed here, so these MUST be ignored, not just
# left untracked — that's how they kept leaking into commits.
.claude/
.claude.json
.codex/
.cursor/
.agents/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
.aider*
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
AGENTS.local.md
GEMINI.md
TODOS.md
TODO.local.md
# Internal design/planning + research notes are local-only; the architecture
# doc docs/runtime-design.md IS tracked (design reference + a test fixture).
docs/superpowers/
docs/research/
ROADMAP.md
/bin/
# A bare `go build` at the repo root drops the binary here; `make` uses /bin/.
/awf
# Local AWF run state: the default --state-dir (runs/, blobs/, live/) that `awf`
# writes when executed in the repo. Per-run output, never an artifact to commit.
.awf/
# Generated man pages (built from man/*.md by `make man`); sources are committed.
man/*.1
man/*.5

# Guard: attackerview-derived CVE pipeline content must NEVER land in this public repo.
# It lives in the separate PRIVATE repo ~/Documents/GitHub/cve-feasibility-awf.
examples/cve-feasibility*
*attackerview*
# Private customer-reproduction material (the "prestige" incident); local only.
Customer's issue/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store

# awf-ui SPA: node deps are local; the built bundle (ui/dist) IS committed and
# embedded via //go:embed (rebuild with `make ui`).
ui/node_modules/

_bmad-output/
_bmad/

# Local agent-tooling state (gstack browse audit log, capability probe cache).
.gstack/
